<BaseLayout title="About">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>
    I'm Chandy. I've spent the last twenty years running operations and
    leading teams across beverage manufacturing, distribution and, more
    recently, steel. Along the way I've hired people I shouldn't have, fixed
    supply chains that were quietly bleeding money, and made calls that took
    me a year to admit were wrong.
  </p>
  <p>
    This site is for the person who just became someone's boss for the
    first time, or is about to. Nobody hands you a manual for that. I write
    about what I've actually seen work on a factory floor and in a
    management meeting, not theory borrowed from a business school I never
    attended.
  </p>
  <p>
    To keep things honest and fair to the companies I've worked with, I
    don't name employers or colleagues here. The situations are real; the
    names are left out.
  </p>
  <p>
    I also run <a href="https://medha-claudeai.com">Medhā Consulting</a>,
    working with small and mid-sized businesses across Southeast Asia on
    the same problems I write about here.
  </p>
  <p>
    New essay every two weeks or so. If you want the next one by email
    rather than checking back, there's a subscribe box at the bottom of
    every post.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
